Ladybird retains the completed rows of a truncated static PNG and leaves
untouched pixels transparent. Blink’s PngImageDecoder uses Skia through
SkiaImageDecoderBase::Decode(), which retains a partially decoded frame.
Gecko’s nsPNGDecoder::row_callback() publishes rows as they arrive.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36 and Firefox 151.0 both drew the reported image.
Firefox filled the missing opaque region differently. WebKit 26.5,
using ImageDecoderCG::setData() and createFrameImageAtIndex(), showed a
transparent image for that file. All three drew a complete image whose
IEND chunk alone was missing.
